#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ns: the Namma Space command line (Mac, Python 3 standard library only).

    ./ns doctor                       ssh, disk, free GPU memory, image digests, Mac tools, timed 100 MB copy
    ./ns sync [subdir]                rsync the code to tyrone (never --delete)
    ./ns check <video> [video...]     preflight on the Mac (pipeline/ingest/check_mac.py)
    ./ns run <video> --name N [--height CM] [--measure what=metres[:method]] [--quick] [--from STAGE] [--to STAGE]
    ./ns run --frames DIR --name N    same, from a folder of photos
    ./ns run tyrone:/path/IMG.MOV --name N   a video (or --frames tyrone:/dir) already on the GPU host: linked, not copied
    ./ns run --name N --from train    resume: nothing is uploaded again, finished stages are skipped
    ./ns status <name>                stage table of a run on tyrone
    ./ns pull <name> [--light|--all]  copy results back to runs/<name>/ (big intermediates excluded)
    ./ns bundle|verify|report <name>  Mac-side steps after a pull
    ./ns serve <name> [--port 5178]   http://127.0.0.1:5178/?scene=<name> from runs/<name>/80_web
    ./ns rescale <name> [--scale K | --use-measures]   new T_final, rebuilt grid and bundle, no retraining
    ./ns package <name>               assemble the Drive folder contents under runs/<name>/package/
    ./ns publish <name>               dry run: lists what would go public. --execute asks for a typed phrase
    ./ns test <pkg|e2e|all> [--remote] run a package's tests (test/unit/<pkg>/ or test/e2e/)

Environment: NS_HOST (default sher@10.1.18.190), NS_REMOTE_ROOT (default /home/sher/namma-space),
NS_LOCAL_RUNS (default ./runs).
Stage runs live on tyrone under runs/<name>/ and survive an ssh drop; `ns run` only polls them.
Exit codes follow CONTRACTS 2.11: 0 good, 10 capture problem, 11 partial, 20 infrastructure, 30 gate failed.
"""
